Title: Power BI Tutorial for Beginners | Power BI Dashboard Project | Power BI Course 2023 Channel: Rishabh Mishra Duration: 44:59

Description

A beginner-level, end-to-end Power BI tutorial that walks through building a full dashboard project in a single video, from installing Power BI Desktop to publishing a finished dashboard with insights. Covers Power BI basics, importing data, Power Query, DAX, data modelling, and building charts/filters into a working dashboard.

What I Learned From the Video
What Power BI is and where it fits as a business intelligence/reporting tool.
How to install Power BI Desktop and navigate the interface (Report, Data, and Model views).
Importing data into Power BI from external files (CSV in this case).
Power Query — how to clean and transform raw data before it's used in reports (removing errors, renaming columns, changing data types).
DAX basics — using DAX to create simple measures and calculations from the data.
Data modelling — setting up relationships between tables so the report can pull connected data correctly.
Building a dashboard — adding charts, filters, and slicers, then arranging them into a clean, readable layout.
Reading insights from a dashboard — how to look at a finished dashboard and pull out the actual business takeaways, not just build visuals for their own sake.

Notes for Myself
This is a project-based tutorial rather than a slide-based course, so it's a good one to revisit hands-on rather than just re-watching.
Power Query and Data Modelling were the two sections most relevant to the "Reporting Analyst" side of my Tool Notes, since these are the steps before a report is ever built.
Worth pairing with the official Microsoft Power BI documentation if I want more detail on DAX functions beyond what's shown here.
